**How the cherry-pick went**
- **Templates, `run.sh` and the new `grpcserver_serve_on.go`:** applied cleanly on every line.
- **`stream_expiry_behavior_test.go` on 2.0–2.3:** the only real conflict was in the import block. Those branches still import `os`, which the file uses for `os.Getenv`. I kept `os`, dropped `strconv`, and the rest of the change applied as on main. 2.4–2.6 merged automatically.
- **Lint test:** on every line I deleted `scripts/cross_test_listener_test.go` and put the test in the new `scripts/cross_test_go_listener_test.go`, with its own header, imports and comment.
- **Commit message:** it keeps a4e9a225's text, then adds a short paragraph saying where the lint test lives on release branches, then the `(cherry picked from commit a4e9a225...)` line, and ends with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`. The original paragraph still says "scripts/cross_test_listener_test.go now also fails…"; the added paragraph right after it gives the correct file name.

**Test results (the same on all seven lines)**
- **(a) Lint test:** `go test -run KeepTheListener -count=1 .` gives `ok github.com/tacplus-dev/tacplus/scripts`. With only the two test files reset to the branch's originals it gives `--- FAIL: TestGoTestsKeepTheListenerTheyBind`, naming both files, so every line has the bug. I restored the files afterwards.
- **(b) Stream-expiry:** `run.sh --language go` ends with `ok …/s2sm/grpc/servers/svc/streamexpiry ~8.3–9.6s` and `==> stream-expiry check PASSED (go)`.
- **(c) Generated keepalive test:** after `go mod tidy` and `go vet` passed, it gives `--- PASS: TestKeepaliveOverrideDoesNotGOAWAYGeneratedClient (140.05–140.10s)` and `ok …/chassis/grpcserver ~141.1s`.

Each PR body follows #538 and has the four sections you asked for. The Changes section explains the different lint test file name and why. Tests gives the commands and their last result lines, and says full `just gates` was not run.

**Other notes**
- `gofmt` flags an import-ordering issue (`x509wrapper`) in `stream_expiry_behavior_test.go` on every line. It is already on the release branches, so I left it alone.
- I removed all seven worktrees; only ignored files were in them. The background runs I started have both finished. I did not touch the main checkout.
